    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.24), who stands as our premier start. His matchup against Castillo represents an ideal synergy of speed-first utility and a favorable platoon advantage (+14%), making him the engine of our stolen base pursuit. Following close behind, **Trea Turner** (73.19), **Junior Caminero** (72.15), and **Kyle Schwarber** (72.52) are all locked into high-leverage spots against Junk; with the opposing pitcher's xERA resting at 4.51, these three provide the necessary power-speed mix to exploit the matchup. **Colt Keith** (61.53) also earns a nod as a strong play, benefiting from a clean platoon advantage that outweighs the minor park penalties he faces against Mlodzinski.\n\nDecisions in the middle of the lineup were dictated by high-upside matchup factors. **Caleb Durbin** (69.02) is a mandatory start despite a 30% rain risk, as his +19% SP skill adjustment against Bratt is too valuable to ignore. On the bench, **Pedro Ramirez** (48.81) was the final cut; while he offers solid versatility, his lower projected efficiency in the #7 hole makes him the odd man out behind our top-six producers. We remain cautious of the weather, specifically with **Lars Nootbaar** and **Hector Rodriguez**, who join **Caleb Durbin** in facing potential precipitation. Should the rain force a late-scratched lineup, we have depth ready to plug the gap to ensure we maximize our daily game caps without sacrificing our core stolen base threats.",
